<div class='mailer__content'>
  <p class='govuk-body'>Dear <%= @user.first_name %>,</p>

  <p class='govuk-body'>You’ve now completed enough CPD to work towards your <%= link_to "Teach primary computing certificate", cms_page_url("primary-certificate"), class: "ncce-link" %> – well done!</p>

  <p class='govuk-body'>This nationally recognised certificate helps show your dedication to professional growth and enhances your teaching confidence and expertise.</p>

  <p class='govuk-body'>To receive your certificate, there’s one final step. You need to submit evidence for each of the two sections on your dashboard:</p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>putting what you’ve learned into practice in the classroom</li>
    <li>sharing what you’ve learned with others</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    <%= link_to "Check your dashboard", primary_certificate_url, class: "govuk-button button" %>
  </p>

  <p class='govuk-body'>You’re probably doing some of these activities as part of your everyday teaching. For example, using NCCE teaching resources in lessons, running or supporting an enrichment activity, reflecting on classroom practice, or progressing through the Computing Quality Framework.</p>

  <p class='govuk-body'>When you visit your <%= link_to "dashboard", primary_certificate_url, class: "ncce-link" %>, you’ll be able to choose activities from a list in each section and see guidance on what evidence to submit.</p>

  <p class='govuk-body'>After submitting evidence for one activity in each section and passing the review, you can claim your Teach primary computing certificate.</p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    <%= link_to "Complete final step", primary_certificate_url, class: "govuk-button button" %>
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body"><strong>Not the right time?</strong></p>
  <p class="govuk-body">If you don't want to continue on the programme at this time, <%= mail_to "info@teachcomputing.org", "let us know", class: "ncce-link" %> and we'll update our records. You can still re-enrol yourself in the future on <%= link_to "our website", primary_certificate_url, class: "ncce-link" %>.</p>
</div>
